WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.400
It's hard with the kids behind you
knowing that they're laughing at you

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.580
*The Yeti laughs*

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:17.420
It's not hard-

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.040
They didn't even notice... they didn't even
notice, they didn't even notice

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.400
Some of the people, they're in the Amsterdam sign, they noticed. They were looking at us a little bit

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.830
Yup! That's okay though.

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:30.830
*music plays*

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:31.870
Goedemorgen

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:33.430
(crowd says) Good morning Hank!

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.600
(Guy with puppet says) Good morning Hank!

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:39.660
Hank, it's Sunday. It's news day and the news today is that I went to Netherlands and I want to tell you about it.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.000
So, Hank, I have just gotten home from a
week of touring Holland with two other

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.780
american authors, Jordan Sonnenblick and
Steve Cougar, and man it was fun!

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:49.410
God I love The Netherlands! I love its
public transportation, the amazingly nice

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:53.370
teachers lounges in its public schools,
its daring architecture, and of course

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:58.610
it's amazing cafes with their brilliant
bitter balls! Bitter balling!

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.680
Oh man Hank, I wish you had taste-o-vision 
so you could know what happens when they

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.480
mix meat and hope and then fry it.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.500
Hmmm, hope.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.840
Oh Hank and also on this trip to The
Netherlands, I discovered a new amazing

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:13.790
Dutch delicacy! Tackenschlacken! By the
way I pretty much made up the name

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:14.840
Hawkinschalkin

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:20.540
It's a Dutch delicacy. It's white bread, butter and, uh,  chocolate sprinkles, so I'm gonna

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:24.960
It's delicious.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:25.520
Really.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:29.980
Some say it's the new bitterballs.

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:34.070
I mean Hank is the poet hath wrote "Ooh,
baby, do you know what that's worth?"

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:38.600
"Ooh, heaven is a place on Earth". And as if
all that weren't enough, on Thursday

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:42.440
night the city of Amsterdam was
inundated with more than 100 made-of-

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:47.450
awesome nerdfighters for an evening of
hilarity, fun, and me epically failing at

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:48.250
reading in Dutch.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:02:01.280
*trying to read in Dutch*

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:08.260
Hank, look! *screams*

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:12.440
Hank, look, wooden shoes with Willy!
He's a pirate!

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.500
When I say "bitter" you say "balls"

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.140
BITTER

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:15.820
BALLS

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:16.320
BITTER

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:16.820
BALLS

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.840
Ooh, Accio Deathly Hallows

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:26.600
I mean, Hank, people were singing a song you wrote in a bar in Amsterdam.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:29.990
Allow me to quote David after his visit
to the dentist.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:36.160
I feel funny. Is this real life? Oh and Hank, one other story I was being interviewed by a journalist in Holland

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.160
and she said she'd read paper towns in both English and Dutch and then she said

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:46.760
"It was much better in Dutch" and then I was like "why?" and she said "much funnier".

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:47.780
So, Nerdfighters, if you can read in Dutch,

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:51.300
you should definitely buy Paper Towns
in Dutch, that way my publisher Lemniscaat

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:55.260
will bring me back over to Holland
and I can eat more bitterballen and more

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:58.440
hawkishshocking and I will live happily
ever after.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.680
Okay Hank, there are a bunch of awesome links,
amsterdam-y and otherwise in the sidebar,

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.710
I will talk to you about the peeps eating
situation on Tuesday and now I have to

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:05.370
go sleep.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:06.490
DFTBA!

